UID:ed1360a7ce78a2b4@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T011642Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Brigade ***\nSoldier
 s: Artillery\, Brigade\, Infantry — Costume (you provide): Black Seaml
 ess Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard Male Soldiers: Black T-shirt\, Black
  tights\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair:
  High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): White Gloves\; Prop (BA
  provides): Brown gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder
  matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease wit
 h an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. 
 No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dan
 cer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red 
 lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone bal
 let shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with car
 e while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly not
 ify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of disco
 very\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessorie
 s on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain f
 rom sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\,
  mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply sta
 ge make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from sm
 udging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use o
 f spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment 
 not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or bevera
 ge while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove cos
 tumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove
  all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\
 n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with
  any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not
  pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or s
 tain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
