  Scene\, Battle Scene\, Snow Scene) (Mandatory – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 9:30 AM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 9:15 AM.\nOn stage: 10:30 AM–11:00 AM.\nACT 
 I Student Matinee Performance (to recorded sound)\; NO COFFEE\, BON BON\
 , ANGELS.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA:
  Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive
  15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\,
  Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehearsals and Perfor
 mances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKE
 UP — Brigade ***\nSoldiers: Artillery\, Brigade\, Infantry — Costume
  (you provide): Black Seamless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard Male Sold
 iers: Black T-shirt\, Black tights\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup:
  Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provide
 s): White Gloves\; Prop (BA provides): Brown gun\nLight Stage Makeup Ins
 truction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shado
 w applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black e
 yeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be 
 sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage li
 ghts)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh ton
 e tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Han
 dle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicat
 e fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume d
 amage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never t
 hrow costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their el
 astic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n
 • Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or a
 ccessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take 
 great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its remova
 l\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume
 \n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not han
 dle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of
  water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or
  from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces 
 and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigne
 d bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ 
 wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or 
 anything that may damage or stain costumes.
